{"id":12443,"date":"2025-06-06T10:16:59","date_gmt":"2025-06-06T10:16:59","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=12443"},"modified":"2025-08-20T12:33:19","modified_gmt":"2025-08-20T12:33:19","slug":"if-i-need-a-project-done-in-a-year-how-soon-should-i-start","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/if-i-need-a-project-done-in-a-year-how-soon-should-i-start\/","title":{"rendered":"If I Need a Project Done in a Year, How Soon Should I Start?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Planning a <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/whole-home-remodeling-2\/\" title=\"\">home remodeling<\/a> or construction project requires careful timing to ensure everything is completed on schedule. If you need your project finished within a year, starting early is crucial\u2014sometimes sooner than you might think. The timeline isn\u2019t just about the construction itself; it also includes planning, design, permits, and potential delays.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are looking for a more in-depth and personal discussion with our team regarding your specific project, feel free to book a hassle free, no obligation 1 on 1 virtual consultation with our Construction Consultant:<a href=\"https:\/\/api.leadconnectorhq.com\/widget\/bookings\/harris-sons-virtual-consultation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"\"> Book a Call.<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here\u2019s a breakdown of why starting early matters and how to calculate the best timeline for your project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com\/docsz\/AD_4nXd05Rdj97IswoOlneYt4R5Nv2s6-oWGs3CVSC8lfUdGZ6v7keCipMRapmF3R4Y7_XGMqlv1F4VLxzF7LGySzpIZEbQSsdgUnKmzhRtJuf-HozfEbGPgr1AkLXTiDp0aIxH6AUEeQQ?key=Jptj_jFu-cv1dXjbg8CbpXwt\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:548px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Factors That Impact Your Timeline<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Project Complexity<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Simple Projects<\/strong>: Minor remodels like painting or fixture replacements may only take a few weeks or months.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Complex Projects<\/strong>: Large-scale remodels, structural changes, or custom builds require extensive planning, permitting, and execution, which can take 6\u201312 months or more.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. The Preconstruction Process<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <strong>Oregon Preconstruction Process<\/strong> involves several steps that can take weeks or even months to complete:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Initial Consultation<\/strong>: Discuss your goals, budget, and vision with your contractor.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Design Development<\/strong>: Create detailed plans and renderings.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Permit Acquisition<\/strong>: Secure necessary permits, especially in cities like Oregon where compliance with <strong>Oregon code<\/strong> and <strong>Oregon permits<\/strong> is critical.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Budget and Timeline Planning<\/strong>: Establish a clear timeline and budget with contingencies for unexpected delays.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This process ensures a smooth start to your project but can take up to 3\u20134 months for complex renovations.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Availability of Contractors<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The best contractors often book months in advance. If you have a specific timeline, securing your contractor early increases the likelihood of completing your project on time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Permitting and Compliance<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Obtaining permits can be a time-consuming process, especially in cities like Oregon where strict regulations apply.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Average Time<\/strong>: Depending on the scope of work, obtaining permits can take anywhere from 2 weeks to 3 months.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Complications<\/strong>: Delays often occur if your project requires additional reviews, such as for historic properties or environmental considerations.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. Material Availability<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Global supply chain issues and seasonal demand can impact the availability and delivery times for materials.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Specialty Items<\/strong>: Custom cabinetry, countertops, or imported tiles may require 2\u20136 months to arrive.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Stock Items<\/strong>: Even standard materials can experience delays during peak seasons.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>6. Seasonal Considerations<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Weather conditions can affect certain types of work, such as roofing, exterior painting, or landscaping. Planning around seasonal limitations ensures your project stays on track.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com\/docsz\/AD_4nXdtmq4U9zN2lKUvlBAev0GjwRhveRuHCCGt-QkpDGip9ZZkZw_ZJg40JvIIpG3ojSY2LMUgktJZCIkYPxB98fLo8BhdRmEjFxHlVAIG4EVIYdKOyozdg1uU7JKsyx7qVdICt51C?key=Jptj_jFu-cv1dXjbg8CbpXwt\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:660px;height:auto\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>When Should You Start?<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you want your project completed within a year, you should start planning <strong>6\u201312 months in advance<\/strong>. Here\u2019s a sample timeline:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>12 Months Before Completion<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Begin the preconstruction process.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hire a contractor and finalize your design plans.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Research and secure financing, such as a HELOC or renovation loan.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>9\u201310 Months Before Completion<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Submit permit applications.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Order long-lead materials like custom cabinetry or specialty finishes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>6\u20138 Months Before Completion<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Finalize the budget and construction timeline.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Begin demolition or preliminary site work.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3\u20135 Months Before Completion<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Major construction phase: framing, electrical, plumbing, and structural work.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Last 1\u20132 Months<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Complete finishing touches like painting, flooring, and installing fixtures.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Conduct inspections and obtain final approvals.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why Starting Early Is Essential<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Avoid Last-Minute Stress<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rushing decisions or skipping steps can lead to mistakes, budget overruns, or dissatisfaction with the final result.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Build Contingency Time<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Starting early allows room for unexpected delays, such as:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Permit backlogs.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Weather disruptions.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Material shortages.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Secure the Best Professionals<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">High-quality contractors are in demand, and starting early ensures their availability for your project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Case Study: A Kitchen Remodel in Portland<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Situation<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A Portland homeowner wanted their kitchen remodel completed by Thanksgiving. They started planning in January.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Process<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>January<\/strong>: Began the preconstruction process, including design development and permit applications.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>March<\/strong>: Secured permits and ordered custom cabinets with a 12-week lead time.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>May<\/strong>: Construction began, including demolition and structural work.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>October<\/strong>: Finishing touches were completed, including painting and appliance installation.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Result<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The project was finished on time, thanks to early planning and a clear timeline.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Role of the Portland Preconstruction Process<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The <a href=\"https:\/\/www.knack.com\/blog\/pre-construction-planning\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Portland Preconstruction Process<\/strong><\/a> is designed to eliminate surprises and ensure your project stays on schedule. It includes:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Comprehensive planning to identify potential delays.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Detailed budgeting to avoid financial surprises.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Proactive permit acquisition to comply with Portland\u2019s regulations.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-id=\"12447\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/03\/create-a-highly-detailed-and-sharp-focus-image-depicting-a-stressful-1-edited.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-12447\"\/><\/figure>\n<\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Tips for Staying on Track<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Start Early<\/strong>: Begin planning as soon as possible\u20146\u201312 months before your desired completion date.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Work with Professionals<\/strong>: Choose contractors familiar with the <strong>Oregon preconstruction process<\/strong> and local regulations.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Be Flexible<\/strong>: Allow room for contingencies and adjustments.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Communicate Clearly<\/strong>: Maintain open communication with your contractor to stay informed about progress and potential delays.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Conclusion: Timing Is Everything<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you need your remodeling project completed within a year, starting early is essential. From planning and permitting to construction and finishing touches, each phase takes time and careful coordination. Leveraging the <strong>Oregon Preconstruction Process<\/strong> ensures your project stays on track, minimizing stress and maximizing results.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\"><strong>Contact Harris &amp; Sons today<\/strong> <\/a>to start planning your remodel. Let\u2019s make your vision a reality\u2014on time and within budget!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\